[1mThe mismatch: exit status on a broken stdout pipe.[22m With no reader on stdout, C is killed by [38;5;10mSIGPIPE[0m (status 141) while Rust exited 0. Cause: the Rust runtime sets [38;5;10mSIGPIPE[0m to [38;5;10mSIG_IGN[0m before [38;5;10mmain[0m, so writes return [38;5;10mEPIPE[0m, and the translation discarded write errors (correct in itself — C's stdio also swallows them). Fixed with [38;5;10msignal(SIGPIPE, SIG_DFL)[0m at the top of [38;5;10mmain[0m, declared through a local [38;5;10mextern "C"[0m block since libc is already linked; no new dependency.[0m[0m
