That bug was only reachable once the test itself was correct. My first version of the SIGPIPE test reported the [3mC[23m program exiting 0, because plain [38;5;10mpipe()[0m fds are not [38;5;10mO_CLOEXEC[0m, so the child inherited the read end of its own stdout pipe and kept a reader alive. Switching to [38;5;10mpipe2(O_CLOEXEC)[0m, and closing the read end while the child is still blocked on stdin, makes it deterministic.[0m[0m
